  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 `RandomForest` passes n_estimators, criterion, max_samples, max_depth and n_jobs only; `random_state` is unset (global numpy stream). The v2 `randomForest` predictor pins `random_state` (an integer; `None` before the working-tree change that sets 42). With `random_state` equal to the integer the global numpy stream is seeded with, the forests are identical.",
    "Default hyperparameters: 1.6.1 first grid point n_estimators=100, max_samples=0.2, max_depth=5, criterion=squared_error, n_jobs=-1 (grid max_depth 5/10/30); v2 declares n_estimators=100, max_samples=0.2, max_depth=15 (space 5..25), criterion=squared_error, n_jobs=-1. Only max_depth differs. B5 should decide whether to match 5.",
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading the CSVs (hyperparameter `gene_list`, a missing gene raises); the v2 preset consumes the whole gene expression view (`scaledGeneExpression` without `gene_list`). The case compares a pre-selected matrix; wiring the list into the preset belongs to B5.",
    "Features agree to float32 precision (class forward): v2 holds them as float32, 1.6.1 as float64. The forests nevertheless have the same structure, because sklearn casts the training matrix to float32 itself and the split order of random data does not change under a 1-ulp perturbation."
